Id: sudo005w
Severity: WARN
Category: accounts
Check: check_sudo
References: sudoers(5)

A file holding sudo's rules (/etc/sudoers, /etc/sudoers.d or a file in
it) is not owned by root, or can be written by its group or by anyone.
Whoever can write those rules can grant themselves root. Recent sudo
versions refuse to use such a file, which then breaks sudo for
everyone instead.

To fix it, 'chown root:root' the file and 'chmod 0440' it (0755 for
the directory), and find out how it got that way.
